{
  "slug": "otto-ads",
  "name": "OTTO Sponsored Product Ads",
  "aliases": [
    "OTTO Ads",
    "OTTO Werbung"
  ],
  "description": "OTTO Market Sponsored Product Ads: campaigns, advertised SKUs (targets), keywords and bids, plus SPA reporting (campaign and product KPIs, CSV reports) for advertisers on otto.de. OAuth 2.0 client credentials with the advertising scope.",
  "region": "de",
  "category": "advertising",
  "icon": "otto-market",
  "docsUrl": "https://api.otto.market/docs/functional-interfaces/sponsored-product-ads",
  "prerequisites": "An OTTO Market partner account that books Sponsored Product Ads, and an app in OTTO Partner Connect with the advertising interface enabled.",
  "instructions": "**Getting credentials**\n1. In **OTTO Partner Connect** create an app for your own account (or open the one you use for the Partner API) and enable the **Sponsored Product Ads** interfaces. You receive a **client id** and a **client secret**.\n2. Set `OTTO_ADS_CLIENT_ID` and `OTTO_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET`. AnythingMCP runs OTTO's client-credentials flow against `https://api.otto.market/v1/token` with the scope `advertising-services`; a token lasts 30 minutes and is fetched again when it expires.\n3. Orders, products, stock and returns are a separate scope and live in the **OTTO Market** connector. Keeping ads apart means an app without the advertising interface keeps working there.\n\n**Money is in euro cents.** Budgets, bids and costs are `{\"amount\": 160, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}` = 1.60 EUR. The minimum bid and budget amount is 20 (0.20 EUR). Report columns `TOTAL_COSTS` and `TOTAL_SALES` are cents too.\n\n**Bids live in two places.** AUTOMATIC campaigns bid per target (SKU); MANUAL campaigns bid per positive keyword. Negative keywords (no bid) work in both and belong to one target: to exclude a search term for a whole campaign, add it to every target.\n\n**Writes are asynchronous.** Every create, update and delete answers `202` with `changeRequest.requestId`. Poll `otto_ads_get_change_request` (wait a second, then double the wait) until `ACCEPTED` or `REJECTED`; a rejection carries `rejectionReason`. Only one change request per campaign may be `PENDING`: a second write to the same campaign before the first is done fails with `409`. A status change to the status a campaign already has is rejected (\"Invalid status transition PAUSED to PAUSED\"), so read the campaign first.\n\n**Paging.** List tools return `nextCursor`; pass it back as `cursor` until it is `null`. `limit` is 1 to 1000 (default 100).\n\n**Reporting.** KPIs cover at most the last 90 days and never today. OTTO attributes sales up to 14 days after the click, including other articles of the same brand (`totalSalesSeller`), so recent days still change. A campaign without impressions in the range answers 404 \"Data not found\". CSV reports: request one, poll `otto_ads_get_report_status` until `READY`, then `otto_ads_download_report`. At most 200 reports per 24 hours across all report types; a file is kept 24 hours.\n\n**Writes change live advertising and spend money**: `otto_ads_create_campaign`, `otto_ads_update_campaign`, `otto_ads_add_targets`, `otto_ads_update_target_bids`, `otto_ads_add_keywords`, `otto_ads_update_keywords`. `otto_ads_delete_keywords` is installed switched off. Confirm amounts with the user before writing.\n\nThe read tools were checked against a live advertiser account; the write tools follow OTTO's documentation and a working production integration.",
  "requiredEnvVars": [
    "OTTO_ADS_CLIENT_ID",
    "OTTO_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET"
  ],
  "envVarMeta": {
    "OTTO_ADS_CLIENT_ID": {
      "label": "Client ID",
      "kind": "credential",
      "help": "OTTO Partner Connect, your app, with the Sponsored Product Ads interfaces enabled.",
      "link": "https://portal.otto.market"
    },
    "OTTO_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET": {
      "label": "Client secret",
      "kind": "credential",
      "help": "Shown once when the app's secret is created; rotate it in OTTO Partner Connect if lost.",
      "link": "https://portal.otto.market"
    }
  },
  "verifyHints": {
    "auth_failed": "OTTO refused the client id or secret, or the app does not have the Sponsored Product Ads interface enabled. Check the app in OTTO Partner Connect."
  },
  "connector": {
    "name": "OTTO Sponsored Product Ads",
    "type": "REST",
    "baseUrl": "https://api.otto.market",
    "authType": "OAUTH2",
    "authConfig": {
      "grant": "client_credentials",
      "clientId": "{{OTTO_ADS_CLIENT_ID}}",
      "clientSecret": "{{OTTO_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET}}",
      "tokenUrl": "https://api.otto.market/v1/token",
      "tokenAuthMethod": "client_secret_post",
      "scope": "advertising-services"
    },
    "headers": {
      "Content-Type": "application/json"
    },
    "healthcheckPath": "/v1/sponsored-product-ads/campaigns?limit=1"
  },
  "probe": {
    "tool": "otto_ads_list_campaigns",
    "params": {
      "limit": 1
    }
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "otto_ads_list_campaigns",
      "description": "List Sponsored Product Ads campaigns: campaignId, name, status (PENDING, WAITING, ACTIVE, PAUSED, ENDED, CANCELED), campaignType (AUTOMATIC or MANUAL), budget (euro cents), budgetType, pacing, start and end date. Page with cursor = nextCursor until it is null.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "limit": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1,
            "maximum": 1000,
            "description": "Campaigns per page, 1 to 1000. Default 100."
          },
          "cursor": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "nextCursor from the previous page. Omit for the first page."
          }
        }
      },
      "endpointMapping": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/v1/sponsored-product-ads/campaigns",
        "queryParams": {
          "limit": "$limit",
          "cursor": "$cursor"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "otto_ads_get_campaign",
      "description": "Read one campaign: status, type, budget (euro cents), budgetType, pacing and dates. Read it before changing its status: setting the status it already has is rejected.",
      "parameters": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "campaign_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "campaignId (UUID) from otto_ads_list_campaigns."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "campaign_id"
        ]
      },
      "endpointMapping": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/v1/sponsored-product-ads/campaigns/{campaign_id}"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "otto_ads_list_targets",
